pnpm lint-staged

# eslint is deliberately not here.
#
# lint-staged runs from the repository root and passes absolute paths. There is
# no root eslint.config.js — each of the nine packages carries its own — so
# `eslint` exited 1 on every commit that touched a .ts file, and the hook took
# the whole commit down with it. The effect was that nobody could commit
# TypeScript from the root at all.
#
# Per-package linting is what `pnpm lint` does (turbo fans it out across all
# nine), and CI runs it on every push. That is the right place for it: a
# monorepo whose configs live per package cannot be linted from one root call.
# prettier stays, because formatting IS root-wide and has a root config.
